===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# {{senseid|en|disease}}{{lb|en|uncountable|disease}} A [[disease#Noun|disease]] [[cause#Verb|caused]] by [[insufficient]] [[intake#Noun|intake]] of [[vitamin C]], [[lead#Verb|leading]] to the [[formation]] of [[livid]] [[spot#Noun|spots]] on the [[skin#Noun|skin]], [[spongy]] [[gum#Noun|gums]], [[loosening#Noun|loosening]] of the [[tooth#Noun|teeth]], and [[bleeding#Noun|bleeding]] into the skin and from almost all [[mucous membrane]]s; {{lb|en|countable|obsolete}} an [[occurrence]] of this disease.
#: {{synonyms|en|Barlow's disease|Cheadle-Möller-Barlow syndrome|Cheadle's disease|Moeller's disease|Möller-Barlow disease|scorbutus}}
#: {{hyponyms|en|land-scurvy|sea-scurvy}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-03
|author=William E. Carter; Merri Sue Carter
|title=The British Longitude Act Reconsidered
|volume=100|issue=2|page=87
|magazine=w:American Scientist
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/the-british-longitude-act-reconsidered
|passage=Conditions were horrendous aboard most British naval vessels at the time. '''Scurvy''' and other diseases ran rampant, killing more seamen each year than all other causes combined, including combat.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|derogatory}} A [[contemptible]] or [[despicable]] [[person#Noun|person]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:git}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|by extension|veterinary disease|obsolete}} A [[cattle]] disease, perhaps [[affect#Verb|affecting]] the skin.

